\title{CMA-ES Acquisition Function Optimizer}
\description{
CMA-ES acquisition function optimizer.
Calls \code{cmaes()} from \CRANpkg{libcmaesr}.
The default algorithm is \code{"abipop"} with unlimited restarts and a budget of \code{100 * D^2} function evaluations,
where \code{D} is the dimension of the search space.
The optimization starts from the best point in the archive.
For the meaning of the control parameters, see \code{libcmaesr::cmaes_control()}.

Only fully numeric search spaces (all parameters of type \code{p_dbl}) are supported.
}
\section{Parameters}{

\describe{
\item{\code{algo}}{\code{character(1)}\cr
CMA-ES variant to use, see \code{libcmaesr::cmaes_algos}.
Default is \code{"abipop"}.}
\item{\code{lambda}}{\code{integer(1)}\cr
Number of generated descendants per iteration.
Deactivate with \code{NA} (Default).}
\item{\code{sigma}}{\code{numeric(1)}\cr
Initial sigma for the covariance.
Deactivate with \code{NA} (Default).}
\item{\code{max_restarts}}{\code{integer(1)}\cr
Maximum number of restarts for the IPOP and BIPOP variants.
Default is \code{1e5}, i.e., restarts are only limited by the evaluation budget.
Deactivate with \code{NA}.}
\item{\code{tpa}}{\code{integer(1)}\cr
Activates or deactivates the two-point adaptation step-size mechanism.
\code{0} for no, \code{1} for auto, \code{2} for yes.
Deactivate with \code{NA} (Default).}
\item{\code{tpa_dsigma}}{\code{numeric(1)}\cr
Value of the two-point adaptation dsigma.
Deactivate with \code{NA} (Default).}
\item{\code{seed}}{\code{integer(1)}\cr
Seed of the random number generator of libcmaes.
If \code{NA} (Default), the seed is drawn from R and the optimization is therefore reproducible via \code{set.seed()}.}
\item{\code{quiet}}{\code{logical(1)}\cr
Should the output of libcmaes be suppressed?
Default is \code{TRUE}.}
\item{\code{skip_already_evaluated}}{\code{logical(1)}\cr
Should the proposed candidate be rejected if it was already evaluated on the actual \link[bbotk:OptimInstance]{bbotk::OptimInstance}?
